{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2183-04-05 21:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee, one of the hospitalists. You're here because of nausea and vomiting that started this morning, is that right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2183-04-05 21:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s right. I was eating cereal with milk, and suddenly I felt very sick and vomited a few times."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2183-04-05 21:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. This feels similar to your past gastroparesis flares, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2183-04-05 21:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Exactly. It’s been years since I’ve had one this bad. I’ve been managing well with diet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2183-04-05 21:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re on a J-tube for meds only, not feeding, and you’ve been eating normally otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2183-04-05 21:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I use the J-tube just for my medications. I haven’t needed tube feeding in years."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2183-04-05 21:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We’ve reviewed your labs from the ER. Your white blood cell count is elevated at 12.5, but you don’t have a fever or signs of infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2183-04-05 21:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that serious? I had high white counts last time too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2183-04-05 21:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s likely a stress response from the flare. Since you’re not running a fever and feel better after treatment, we don’t think it’s an infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2183-04-05 21:27:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That makes sense. I did get Zofran and fluids in the ER and started feeling better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2183-04-05 21:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll continue IV fluids and anti-nausea meds. We also did a J-tube study to make sure it’s in good position."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2183-04-05 21:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And is it okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2183-04-05 21:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the tube is patent and in the right place—tip in the duodenum, with contrast flowing into the jejunum. No issues there."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2183-04-05 21:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good to hear. I was worried it might be blocked or moved."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2183-04-05 21:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No signs of that. We’ll keep you NPO for now and slowly advance your diet tomorrow if you stay symptom-free."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2183-04-06 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2183-04-06 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Much better. I haven’t felt nauseous since last night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2183-04-06 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. Your repeat labs this morning show your white count has dropped to 7.2, which is normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2183-04-06 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a big improvement. What about the other labs?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2183-04-06 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your electrolytes are stable. We also checked your thyroid function—your TSH is 4.3, which is a bit high."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2183-04-06 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m on levothyroxine. Wasn’t it normal last time?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2183-04-06 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it was normal during your last admission. The elevated TSH now might be contributing to your gastroparesis flare."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2183-04-06 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So could my thyroid be making my stomach worse?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2183-04-06 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, hypothyroidism can slow digestion. We’re increasing your levothyroxine from 100 to 125 mcg daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2183-04-06 08:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll take it in the morning on an empty stomach, like always."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2183-04-06 08:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. We’ll also start you on a clear liquid diet and see how you tolerate it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2183-04-06 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "How’s the clear liquid diet going?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2183-04-06 12:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No nausea. I had broth and apple juice, and I feel fine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2183-04-06 12:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s excellent. We’ll advance you to a soft, low-fat diet for dinner."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2183-04-06 18:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You tolerated the soft diet well. No vomiting or discomfort?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2183-04-06 18:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "None at all. I even had a small portion of mashed potatoes and chicken."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2183-04-06 18:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great progress. We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow morning if you continue to do well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2183-04-06 18:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good news. What should I do at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2183-04-06 18:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue small, low-fat, low-dairy meals. Avoid large portions. Stick to your meds, especially the new thyroid dose."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2183-04-06 18:50:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Should I consider using the J-tube for feeding again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2183-04-06 18:51:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s something to discuss with your GI doctor. Since your tube is working, using it a few days a week might help prevent future flares."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2183-04-07 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done really well. Vital signs are stable, you’ve eaten a regular diet, and labs are normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2183-04-07 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel ready to go home. Thank you for helping me through this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2183-04-07 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’re discharging you with instructions to follow up with your PCP in 6 weeks to check your TSH."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2183-04-07 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my gastroenterologist for the J-tube feeding discussion?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2183-04-07 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, exactly. Call us if nausea returns or you can’t keep fluids down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2183-04-07 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again, Dr. Lee."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2183-04-07 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. You’re cleared to go home now."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2183-04-05 21:18:00",
    "admission_end": "2183-04-07 11:22:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of gastroparesis and a J-tube presented with acute nausea and vomiting after eating cereal with milk, consistent with a gastroparesis flare. She was admitted for symptom management and received IV fluids and anti-nausea medications. Her white blood cell count was initially elevated but normalized during the stay, attributed to a stress response. A J-tube study confirmed the tube was patent and correctly positioned. Her TSH was found to be elevated at 4.3, prompting an increase in levothyroxine dose from 100 to 125 mcg daily. She tolerated advancement to a regular diet and was discharged home in stable condition with plans to follow up on thyroid function and discuss potential intermittent J-tube feeding with her GI specialist.",
    "problems": [
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Unspecified acquired hypothyroidism",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Anxiety state, unspecified",
      "Personal history of malignant neoplasm of breast",
      "Attention to other artificial opening of digestive tract"
    ]
  }
}
